# question: For our patients who underwent specific medical procedures during their hospital stay, I need to understand the typical length of time these interventions took. Could you provide the average duration from start to finish, along with the shortest and longest recorded times in days? This will help us benchmark our procedural efficiency for blood cancers and other major conditions.
# expected_compliant: true
# expected_rules: none
# origin: train
# notes: PREFIX sphn: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn#> PREFIX bif: <bif:> SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?r) AS ?records) (COUNT(DISTINCT ?g) AS ?patients) (ROUND(AVG(?d)) AS ?avg_days) (MIN(?d) AS ?min_days) (MAX(?d) AS ?max_days) WHERE { GRAPH ?g { ?r a sphn:MedicalProcedure . ?r sphn:hasStartDateTime ?start ; sphn:hasEndDateTime ?end . } FILTER(?end >= ?start) BIND(bif:datediff("day", ?start, ?end) AS ?d) }
PREFIX sphn: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn#>
PREFIX bif: <bif:>
SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?r) AS ?records) (COUNT(DISTINCT ?g) AS ?patients) (ROUND(AVG(?d)) AS ?avg_days) (MIN(?d) AS ?min_days) (MAX(?d) AS ?max_days) WHERE { GRAPH ?g { ?r a sphn:MedicalProcedure . ?r sphn:hasStartDateTime ?start ; sphn:hasEndDateTime ?end . } FILTER(?end >= ?start) BIND(bif:datediff("day", ?start, ?end) AS ?d) }
